<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Though the net surplus position for banks in the month of November is not very large, the release of 22,000 million rupees by way of CRR reduction will entirely go in chasing assets and yields on gilts are likely to fall further. The turnover in the gilt edged market has been 120,000 million rupees in the month of October, with daily average volumes being 4,780 million rupees, up from 30,000 million rupees and 1,470 million rupees respectively in June. These figures give an indication of the hectic activity seen last month, though the activity gathered momentum only in the second fortnight of October in the run-up to the Credit Policy.</p>
<p>Some hardening in call money rates can be expected in the second fortnight of November as the cash balances released get fully invested and the Reserve Bank's OMO and probably a gilt issue absorb liquidity from the system.</p>
